.TH UNHEADED\-REMEDIATE 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 86590d34" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
unheaded\-remediate \- Remediation as code (ADR\-099): list, check, plan, apply and undo fixes from the model or a sealed snapshot.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unheaded\-remediate
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
list | check <fix> | plan <fix> | apply <fix> | undo <backup\-dir>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remediation as code (ADR\-099): list, check, plan, apply and undo fixes from the model or a sealed snapshot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-applied\-by \fISTRING\fR
with \-record\-existing: what applied the fix, and when (default "remediate.sh (2026\-10\-01)")
.TP
.B \-\-host \fISTRING\fR
host the content is for (default: short hostname)
.TP
.B \-\-model \fISTRING\fR
fix model (root\-owned when run as root) (default /usr/share/unheaded/remediation/fixes.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-model\-commit \fISTRING\fR
git commit of the model, recorded in the journal
.TP
.B \-\-pubkey \fISTRING\fR
ML\-DSA\-65 public key that must have sealed the snapshot (default /etc/unheaded/compliance/snapshot.pub)
.TP
.B \-\-record\-existing \fISTRING\fR
journal this fix as applied before the journal existed, if check finds it in place; changes nothing on the host
.TP
.B \-\-root \fISTRING\fR
filesystem root (tests)
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot \fISTRING\fR
sealed snapshot to act on instead of \-model (only its fixes can be applied)
.TP
.B \-\-state \fISTRING\fR
backups and journal (default /var/lib/unheaded/remediate)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
